---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TesseractHero from '../components/TesseractHero.astro';
import Showcase from '../components/Showcase.astro';
import { HERO_STAGES } from '../scripts/hero-timeline';
import { MACHINING_OPS } from '../scripts/machining-timeline';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="AI-first CAD for engineers"
  description="MIT-licensed, AI-first CAD for engineers. A team of agents collaborates across your workspace and leaves a human-editable feature history. Free desktop and self-hosted software; optional paid hosting supports the project."
>
  <header class="home-hero">
    <div class="wrap home-hero-grid">
      <div class="home-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">MIT-licensed parametric CAD · Desktop and browser</p>
        <h1>AI-first CAD for engineers.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Describe the change you want. A team of agents works across your workspace — sketching, features, measurement, simulation, CAM — and leaves behind a human-editable feature history: fully defined sketches, named relations, and the critical dimensions you specified.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">This AI workflow requires a configured desktop copilot runtime and your own provider account or API key. Online Copilot is not available in the browser deployment.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/download/">Get started</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/self-hosting/">Self-host in your browser</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="home-hero-facts" aria-label="Product fundamentals">
          <li>Exact B-rep solids</li>
          <li>Dimension-driven models</li>
          <li>A team of agents, not a chat window</li>
          <li>MIT licensed; free to run yourself</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <TesseractHero />
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section home-ai" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI in the engineering loop</p>
        <h2 id="ai-title">Describe the change. A team of agents does the work.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Brief the copilot like you'd brief a group of engineers. The agents split the job — one sketches, one builds features, one measures and checks — using the same tools you use by hand, in the document you have open. Everything they build lands in your feature tree, fully defined and yours to edit.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/ai-copilot/">Read the AI copilot guide</a></div>
      </header>
      <ol class="home-ai-steps" aria-label="AI copilot workflow">
        <li><span>1</span><div><strong>Connect</strong><p>Sign in with your AI provider account, or paste an API key. Usage runs on your provider account under its terms.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>2</span><div><strong>Describe</strong><p>Name the part, the change, the critical dimensions, and what must not move.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>3</span><div><strong>Review</strong><p>Open the feature tree. Every sketch is fully defined, every relation is named, every critical dimension is the one you asked for. Save a revision, or send it back.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Showcase
    kind="hero"
    panelTitle="FeatureManager"
    panelDoc="bracket_v4.chud"
    rows={HERO_STAGES}
    kernel="Exact solids"
    activeVerb="Rebuilding"
    doneText="Rebuild complete"
    image={{ src: '/images/modeling.png', width: 1600, height: 900, alt: 'Chudware modeling workspace with a parametric enclosure and editable feature tree' }}
    caption="Feature sequence · illustration"
  >
    <p class="eyebrow">Dimension-driven models</p>
    <h2>Change a dimension. The part rebuilds.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Every model is dimension-driven: fully defined sketches, named relations, and driving dimensions feed an ordered feature tree. Change one value and the extrudes, fillets, holes, and pockets downstream rebuild in order — nothing gets baked into dead geometry.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/product/modeling/">Explore modeling</a></div>
  </Showcase>

  <Showcase
    kind="machining"
    flip
    panelTitle="Operations"
    panelDoc="bracket_v4 · Setup1"
    rows={MACHINING_OPS}
    kernel="Dexel stock · 384 × 262"
    activeVerb="Running"
    doneText="Simulation complete"
    image={{ src: '/images/cam.png', width: 1600, height: 900, alt: 'Chudware manufacturing workspace with stock, operations, and toolpath simulation' }}
    caption="Stock removal · illustration"
  >
    <p class="eyebrow">Manufacturing</p>
    <h2>Review the cut before it reaches the machine.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Build the CAM job from the part you just modeled. Define stock, tools, and operations, watch the stock get cut away, and post G-code for one specific machine.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/product/cam/">Explore CAM</a></div>
  </Showcase>

  <section class="section home-capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One engineering environment</p>
        <h2 id="capabilities-title">One project, from first sketch to released revision.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Every workspace works on the same document and the same revision history. Nothing is exported into a side file that drifts.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article><p class="capability-index">01</p><h3><a href="/product/modeling/">Modeling</a></h3><p>Dimension-driven models on exact B-rep solids. Fully defined sketches, ordered features, all human-editable.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">02</p><h3><a href="/product/assemblies/">Assemblies</a></h3><p>Locate components with mates, then inspect motion, clearance, and interference.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">03</p><h3><a href="/product/simulation/">Simulation</a></h3><p>Static, contact, modal, thermal, buckling, and fatigue studies on the live design — with mesh and equilibrium evidence in the result.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">04</p><h3><a href="/product/cam/">CAM</a></h3><p>Stock, tools, operations, stock-removal simulation, and posted G-code.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">05</p><h3>Electronics</h3><p>ECAD and firmware live in the same project as the mechanical design.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">06</p><h3><a href="/product/plm/">PLM</a></h3><p>Revisions with notes, project files, manufacturing output, and the decision trail in one place.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">07</p><h3><a href="/docs/ai-copilot/">AI</a></h3><p>A team of agents reads your model, builds real features across the workspace, and hands you a human-editable feature tree.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section home-work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading home-work-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Product gallery</p>
          <h2 id="work-title">What the workspaces look like.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/gallery/">Open the gallery</a>
      </header>
      <div class="home-work-grid">
        <figure>
          <a href="/gallery/#modeling"><img src="/images/modeling.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware modeling workspace showing a parametric enclosure and its editable feature tree" /></a>
          <figcaption><span><strong>Modeling</strong> · Editable feature history</span><a href="/gallery/#modeling">Request and result</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <a href="/gallery/#cam"><img src="/images/cam.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware manufacturing workspace with a CAM job, operations, and toolpath simulation" /></a>
          <figcaption><span><strong>CAM</strong> · Operations and toolpath simulation</span><a href="/gallery/#cam">View full image</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <a href="/gallery/#simulation"><img src="/images/fea.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware simulation workspace with a static stress result, legend, and result summary" /></a>
          <figcaption><span><strong>Simulation</strong> · Static stress result</span><a href="/gallery/#simulation">View full image</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
      <h2>Run it yourself, or ask about hosting.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Clone the public MIT source and run Chudware yourself, without a software fee or license key. Public desktop installers are not yet available; the self-hosting guide builds the browser deployment from source. Optional paid, owner-operated hosting supports the project.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/self-hosting/">Start self-hosting</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/contact/">Ask about hosting</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
